; Sweep: every ESP32-S3 PIE intrinsic selects, and selects onto the right
; operands. One function per intrinsic, checked against the full printed operand
; list of the instruction the custom inserter emits.
;
; Derived from the fork's test of the same name (espressif/llvm-project
; release/esp_22.x, llvm/test/CodeGen/Xtensa/xtensa-s3-dsp.ll), not ported from
; it: the fork calls all 252 intrinsics from one function and checks the mnemonic
; alone, which passes unchanged when two same-class operands are swapped in the
; inserter -- and in ~190 of the 214 inserter cases there are two same-class
; operands to swap. So the IR here is regenerated instead, with
;
;   - every q-register operand of a call a distinct number, counting up from q2,
;     so any positional swap of two q operands changes the asm (and a dropped
;     operand shows up as q0),
;   - every immediate operand of a call a legal value for its operand class that
;     is distinct from every other immediate AND from every q number in the same
;     call, so a swap between a q operand and an immediate is visible too,
;   - one function per intrinsic, taking its address-register and float operands
;     as arguments so they land in the fixed argument registers of the windowed
;     ABI: a materialised constant would be placed by the register allocator and
;     the checks below pin the register.
;
; Those three properties are the convention a new intrinsic added here follows;
; the CHECK lines are then regenerated by the command in the NOTE line above.
;
; Operand-shape coverage with explanatory comments, and mnemonic-only checks that
